      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In its early years Roosevelt served as a shipping point for feed and supplies to local sheep and goat ranchers.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        22
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/roosevelt-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "During the 1920s ranchers in Roosevelt bred polo ponies for national markets and horses for the U.S. Cavalry, hosting polo matches.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        24
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/roosevelt-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The same decade saw Hill Country tourism grow, with businesses like the Luthringer Hotel opening to welcome visitors.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
